"""Concise interview answers grounded in the current local evidence."""
from pathlib import Path
from run_completion_and_pairs import read
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def build():
 c=read(ROOT/'output/current_study_06/summary.json');g=c['grader'];cost=c['cost']
 qa=[
 ('What exactly are you selling?', 'A proposed private, permissioned diagnostic collection: 30 fresh task families, three workflow versions each, with native expert deliverables, evidence maps, rationales and preferences. Start with five development families to measure authoring/review cost. The public development tasks are not the product for resale.'),
 ('What is your strongest observed result?', 'The project owner judged two specific historical purchasing issues to require material correction. One assured continuity without a known stock quantity; the other introduced an approval exception inconsistent with the stated rule. These are issue-only observations, not an acceptance rate or a reproducible failure prevalence.'),
 ('Why did you compare five models?', 'That was an engineering exercise and is excluded from the submission leaderboard. Native-file harness built and validated; first live pass failed mainly on provider errors. The focused study fixes one Claude model across five matched baseline/conflict family pairs.'),
 ('Did the paired run establish the effect of conflict?', f"It completed {c['paired_finished_attempts']}/10 attempts with {c['paired_submitted_attempts']} native submissions. Human business outcomes remain unreviewed. Both versions already contain approved and draft workspace records. The contrast changes foreground facts or references and sometimes adds copied notes; it does not isolate conflict presence alone. These inspected development families are not held out."),
 ('Is the grader valid?', f"The approved batch has {g['received']}/56 responses and {g.get('valid_evidence_responses',0)} responses meeting raw evidence-format checks. All 36 constructed responses passed those checks, but only 11/19 historical-output responses did; eight had unverified output quotes and one request failed. Constructed labels are author expectations; format validation is not semantic validation. No full-output human agreement estimate is available. Report missed errors and false accepts with denominators once human reviews exist."),
 ('Could Claude grading Claude explain the result?', 'The new judge is Gemini, which adds model-family diversity but does not establish truth or remove all correlated biases. Historical judge disagreement and all-negative agreement are documented separately. Human comparison and independent reviewer agreement are still required.'),
 ('How do you prevent reward hacking?', 'Use substantive mutations, identical and cosmetic controls, cross-file contradictions, authorized proceed cases and justified holds. Require exact source/output evidence plus competing evidence. Keep quote matching separate from whether the evidence supports the conclusion; never reward checklists or fact copying alone.'),
 ('Where was data generated, and what was the seed?', 'Current scenarios were authored and versioned locally from three public GDPval task derivatives and two constructed families. No teacher API generated the business source facts. Approved records and proposals define truth and distractors; models generate the deliverables. The seed shuffles run order only, and the scenario clock is fixed. It is not a model-generation seed.'),
 ('How did you avoid evaluation contamination?', 'Private maps, reference answers and review labels are outside solver-tool access. No training ran. That prevents direct harness leakage but cannot exclude public pretraining exposure. For the proposed private collection, split complete source/template lineages before training generation and reserve untouched families for final decisions.'),
 ('Which failure would more training data fix?', 'None is proven data-addressable yet. First repair task defects, prompts, tools and budgets. Only verified residual failures become candidates for training data. Persistent failure does not prove data is the only solution; evaluate any intervention on fresh separate families.'),
 ('How would you choose a model?', 'Agree a consequential-error ceiling and minimum useful acceptance before evaluation. Among configurations meeting those gates with adequate evidence, choose the lowest total cost per accepted deliverable. Include generation, retries, judging, tools and measured human correction time. No model qualifies on the current evidence.'),
 ('What did this cost?', f"Provider-reported cumulative API charges are ${cost['reported_cumulative_usd']:.4f}; {cost['unresolved_charge_records']} request-charge records remain unresolved. Human review and correction costs are not measured. This is not a reconciled invoice, account balance or demonstrated customer ROI."),
 ('Who is the expert, and is the taxonomy reproducible?', 'The owner volunteered to review, but purchasing qualifications and independence are unspecified. Two issue-only labels and earlier uncertain answers are not complete expert acceptance labels. Independent double-review and adjudication remain necessary; the proposed taxonomy is assistant triage until manually confirmed.'),
 ('What did the coding agent contribute?', 'Implementation of native tools, extraction, tests, evidence maps, cost logging, orchestration and packaging, plus draft analysis and taxonomy. It did not perform the owner\'s manual review, grant commercial rights, establish domain expertise, train a better model or obtain lab endorsement.'),
 ]
 text='15-MINUTE RESEARCHER DEFENSE\n\nUse the evidence limits directly. Do not turn hypotheses into results.\n\n'
 text+='\n\n'.join(f'{i}. {q}\n{a}' for i,(q,a) in enumerate(qa,1))+'\n'
 dest=ROOT/'output/current_study_06/interview-defense.txt';dest.write_text(text);return dest
if __name__=='__main__':build()
